    "result_text": "All green \u2014 `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` and `BUILD SUCCESS`. The runtime log confirms the new behaviour:\n\n- `memberId=NSW264495D9B46` \u2014 region prefix stays the plain `NSW`\n- audit line: `{\"schemaVersion\":2,...,\"ownerSegment\":\"STANDARD_METRO\",\"event\":\"OWNER_CREATED\"}`\n\n## What I changed\n\n**Version 2 identity, centralized.** New `IdentityVersion` holds the single `\"V2\"` tag plus `API_VERSION`/`AUDIT_SCHEMA_VERSION`, and exposes `tag(preimage)` \u2014 the one place that mixes the tag into an identifier's hash preimage. Each identifier now routes its preimage through it, so all three change and none can collide with a v1 value:\n- `MemberId.hash8` now hashes the tagged **region + telephone + lastName** (the region is now *used inside* the identifier), while the visible `REGION` prefix stays plain.\n- `Household.id` hashes the tagged name+postcode.\n- `IdentityKey.of` hashes the tagged telephone|email|soundex.\n\n**Plain region preserved.** Because the memberId's region *prefix* is unchanged, `MemberId.region(...)` still reads back `NSW`, so `locality`, `timezone` and the owner segment's derived region stay plain automatically \u2014 no change needed there. The tag lives only inside the hashes.\n\n**Response shape** (`openapi.yml` + `OwnerMapper`): the three identifiers moved out of the top level into a new nested `Identity` schema (`identity` object); added a top-level integer `apiVersion` = 2. The mapper builds the `IdentityDto` and reports the version via small dedicated methods; the reusable `identityKey(owner)` helper feeds the nested object.\n\n**Audit event** (`OwnerCreatedEvent`): added `schemaVersion` (= `AUDIT_SCHEMA_VERSION`, 2) and an `ownerSegment` recomputed from the v2 identity (`OwnerSegment.of(level, MemberId.region(memberId))`), reusing existing logic rather than duplicating it.\n\nRequest fields are untouched. Each change lives in the class that already owns that responsibility.",
