    "probe_text": "I've read the endpoint's YAML pipeline and all 24 step classes. Here's what happens, in execution order, for `POST /api/owners`.\n\n## Gate (before any step)\n\n- **Authorization** \u2014 `composition.authorize: hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')` guards the whole file. Callers without that role are rejected (403) before the pipeline runs.\n\nEvery step below runs under `govern: [ transaction ]`, so all DB work commits once at the end; any escalation rolls the whole thing back.\n\n## The pipeline\n\n1. **`recall` \u2014 RecallIdempotentOwner** *(side-effect + short-circuit)*: reads the optional `Idempotency-Key` header. If that key already produced an owner \u2192 throws `IdempotentReplayException` (replays the original owner, skipping everything below). Otherwise publishes the key for later recording.\n\n2. **`validate` \u2014 ValidateOwnerFields** *(validation)*: binds the request body (`@RequestBody` \u2014 the one and only body read). Requires non-blank `firstName`, `lastName`, an address (either structured `addressLine1` **or** flat `address`), `city`, and `telephone`. Reports **all** missing fields together via `MissingOwnerFieldsException` (400). Publishes the validated body.\n\n3. **`ensureRegistrationDate` \u2014 EnsureRegistrationDateNotFuture** *(validation)*: if a `registrationDate` is supplied and is after today \u2192 `FutureRegistrationDateException` (400). Omitted date is allowed.\n\n4. **`ensurePostcode` \u2014 EnsureValidPostcode** *(validation)*: postcode is optional; if present it must be a well-formed 4-digit code **and** valid for the city's region, else `InvalidPostcodeException` (400).\n\n5. **`normalize` \u2014 NormalizeOwnerTelephone** *(validation + side-effect)*: rewrites `telephone` to canonical E.164 in place; unparseable \u2192 `InvalidTelephoneException` (400).\n\n6. **`normalizeEmail` \u2014 NormalizeOwnerEmail** *(validation + side-effect)*: email optional; if present, trims + lower-cases it and validates syntax, else `InvalidEmailException` (400). Mutates the body.\n\n7. **`ensureEmailNotDisposable` \u2014 EnsureEmailNotDisposable** *(validation)*: if email present and its domain is on the disposable blocklist \u2192 `DisposableEmailDomainException` (400).\n\n8. **`normalizeAddress` \u2014 NormalizeOwnerAddress** *(side-effect)*: canonicalizes `addressLine1`/`addressLine2` (trim, collapse, upper-case, expand abbreviations) and rewrites the flat `address` to the composed form.\n\n9. **`ensureCityCapacity` \u2014 EnsureCityHasCapacity** *(validation)*: if the city already holds \u2265 50 owners (case-insensitive) \u2192 `CityAtCapacityException` (409).\n\n10. **`ensureDailyLimit` \u2014 EnsureDailyOwnerLimit** *(validation)*: if \u2265 100 owners already registered on today's business day \u2192 `DailyOwnerLimitException` (429).\n\n11. **`build` \u2014 BuildOwner** *(side-effect)*: maps the DTO to a new `Owner` entity and publishes it. Subsequent steps mutate this entity.\n\n12. **`assignHousehold` \u2014 AssignHousehold** *(side-effect)*: if a postcode is present, stamps `householdId` (derived from last name + postcode); no postcode \u2192 left unstamped.\n\n13. **`ensureUniqueIdentity` \u2014 EnsureUniqueIdentity** *(validation)*: computes an identity key (normalized telephone, email, Soundex of last name); if it matches any non-deleted existing owner \u2192 `DuplicateIdentityException` (409). Soft-deleted owners are skipped.\n\n14. **`flagPossibleDuplicate` \u2014 FlagPossibleDuplicate** *(side-effect)*: sets `possibleDuplicateOf` to the earliest-created (lowest-id) non-deleted owner sharing postcode + phonetic last name but a different identity key. Owner is still created.\n\n15. **`resolveRegistrationDate` \u2014 ResolveOwnerRegistrationDate** *(side-effect)*: defaults `registrationDate` to today if none was given, then rolls a weekend date forward to the following Monday.\n\n16. **`assignMemberId` \u2014 AssignMemberId** *(side-effect)*: computes `memberId` (`<REGION><FY><HASH8><CHK>`) from region/fiscal-year/telephone/last name, de-duplicating against existing member ids by appending `-<n>`.\n\n17. **`countNamesakes` \u2014 CountNamesakes** *(side-effect)*: sets `namesakeCount` to the number of existing owners sharing first + last name (case-insensitive; the new owner isn't counted, since it's not yet saved).\n\n18. **`assignMembershipLevel` \u2014 AssignMembershipLevel** *(side-effect)*: computes and stores `membershipPoints` and a derived `membershipLevel`, capping the level to at most one above the highest level already in the household (uncapped if the household has no existing member).\n\n19. **`save` \u2014 SaveOwner** *(side-effect)*: persists the owner via the repository (now carries its id).\n\n20. **`record` \u2014 RecordIdempotentOwner** *(side-effect)*: associates the `Idempotency-Key` (from step 1) with the new owner id so a repeat replays it. A request with no key records nothing.\n\n21. **`enqueueWelcome` \u2014 EnqueueWelcomeNotification** *(side-effect)*: logs one line to the `NOTIFY` logger (owner id + memberId).\n\n22. **`audit` \u2014 AuditOwnerCreated** *(side-effect)*: logs a human-readable line to the `AUDIT` logger (id, memberId, registrationDate, membershipPoints, membershipLevel).\n\n23. **`auditEvent` \u2014 AuditOwnerCreatedEvent** *(side-effect)*: publishes the immutable structured create event (monotonic sequence + JSON) via `OwnerCreatedEventPublisher`.\n\n24. **`respond` \u2014 RespondWithOwnerCreated** *(side-effect)*: builds the `OwnerDto` and sends `201 Created` with a `Location: /api/owners/{id}` header.\n\n## Notes on ordering\n\n- The **idempotency replay check runs before everything** (even validation), so a repeated key returns the original owner without re-validating.\n- **Validation is deliberately front-loaded** (steps 2\u201310, plus the duplicate-identity check at 13) so bad requests fail before the entity is built and persisted.\n- Both docstrings in `ValidateOwnerFields` and `EnsureRegistrationDateNotFuture` call themselves \"first step,\" but per the YAML the actual first step is `recall`; that wording is stale."
